# =============================================================================
# corporate-sso (INT-046) - federation trust material. DEVELOPMENT PLACEHOLDERS
# ONLY: real values live in the secret store and are injected as env vars; they
# are never written in code (R01-AUDIT). A tenant whose variables are unset or
# invalid cannot log in at all - the broker fails closed.
# =============================================================================

# --- OIDC tenants: HMAC client secrets (HS256 => at least 32 bytes) -----------
FIX_SSO_ROBI_SHARED_SECRET=dev-only-placeholder-robi-hmac-secret-change-me
FIX_SSO_WALTON_SHARED_SECRET=dev-only-placeholder-walton-hmac-secret-change-me

# --- SAML tenants: IdP signing certificate + its SHA-256 pin -----------------
# FIX_SSO_GP_IDP_CERT_PEM holds the PEM text of the IdP signing certificate
# taken from the IdP metadata (multi-line value, -----BEGIN CERTIFICATE----- ...).
# FIX_SSO_GP_IDP_CERT_SHA256 is that certificate's SHA-256 fingerprint (64 hex
# digits; ':' separators and case are ignored), obtained out-of-band from the
# client. Leave both empty locally unless you run a test IdP: SAML login for the
# tenant is then refused with a clear configuration error.
FIX_SSO_GP_IDP_CERT_PEM=
FIX_SSO_GP_IDP_CERT_SHA256=
